{"id": "3ac55237-9bc7-47c6-b8f8-3fb3f4e9f748", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The cause is that AmazonS3ReadOnlyAccess doesn't grant kms:Decrypt permissions, so even with S3 access the role can't decrypt KMS-encrypted objects. The key policy would need to explicitly allow the role or delegate to IAM for an attached policy to have any effect.

I should also mention other potential issues like cross-account/region mismatches, VPC endpoint restrictions, wrong ModelDataUrl paths, SCPs, or ECR pull permissions, while noting I can't confirm without more data. I'll recommend CLI commands like describe-endpoint, head-object to check SSEKMSKeyId, get-key-policy, and simulate-principal-policy, plus checking CloudTrail for KMS AccessDenied events — keeping the response concise and read-only.

